functions.remarks:
This is a "logical" resource that groups multiple `MongoDBServerResource` instances that are annotated as members of the replica set.
The replica set is initialized by the AppHost itself, which is something that only happens when running locally.
Publishing and deploying an application that contains a MongoDB replica set is therefore not supported yet and
this method throws when the AppHost runs in publish mode.
```
var mongo1 = builder.AddMongoDB("mongo-1");
var mongo2 = builder.AddMongoDB("mongo-2");
var replicaSet = builder.AddMongoDBReplicaSet("rs0")
.WithMember(mongo1)
.WithMember(mongo2);
```
